# Git hygiene (always apply)

- Format: `<type>: <short description>` (feat, fix, refactor, docs, chore, test).
- One line in the subject when possible; no commit body unless strictly necessary.
- Never add `Co-authored-by`, `Co-Authored-By`, or similar trailers. If the IDE adds them, remove before `git commit` finishes.
- Human-like wording: say what changed in plain language. Prefer commas or "and" over em dash `—`. Avoid hype verbs (harden, leverage, streamline, robust, comprehensive).
- After commit, verify: `git log -1 --format=%B` must not contain co-author lines.
- Install enforcement once: `scripts/install-git-hooks.sh` (pre-commit rejects trailers and `—` in the subject).
- Never commit `ProjectMemory.json5`, `.credentials.env`, or `.cursor-agent-backups/`.